WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.997
Axis is one of the most important concepts in NumPy.

00:00:03.997 --> 00:00:11.942
In a two-dimensional array, axis zero works down the rows and produces one result for each column.

00:00:11.942 --> 00:00:17.490
Axis one works across the columns and produces one result for each row.

00:00:17.981 --> 00:00:22.003
A simple way to remember this is to think about what disappears.

00:00:22.003 --> 00:00:28.508
If we sum using axis zero, the row dimension is collapsed, so we get column totals.

00:00:28.508 --> 00:00:35.143
If we sum using axis one, the column dimension is collapsed, so we get row totals.

00:00:35.143 --> 00:00:38.673
Always connect the axis to the meaning of the data.

00:00:38.673 --> 00:00:47.358
If rows are products and columns are months, axis zero can summarize by month, while axis one can summarize by product.
